WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.792
How Claude Code does all of this.

2
00:00:02.072 --> 00:00:06.616
You have used Claude Code for a year, so here is the same machinery in the tool you know.

3
00:00:06.896 --> 00:00:07.664
CLAUDE.

4
00:00:07.944 --> 00:00:09.437
md is the up-front half.

5
00:00:09.717 --> 00:00:11.232
Claude Code loads CLAUDE.

6
00:00:11.512 --> 00:00:22.008
md files (project, user, and organization scopes) at the start of every session, in full, on every request, where prompt caching keeps the repeat cost down.

7
00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:35.003
The docs suggest keeping each file under 200 lines, because longer files cost context and reduce adherence, and moving instructions that apply to only part of a codebase into path-scoped rules under.

8
00:00:35.283 --> 00:00:40.019
claude/rules/, which load only when Claude works on matching files.

9
00:00:40.299 --> 00:00:46.805
@path imports help organize a file but do not reduce its cost, because imported files load with it.

10
00:00:47.085 --> 00:00:50.989
Auto memory is the note-taking half: Claude writes its own MEMORY.

11
00:00:51.269 --> 00:00:56.027
md, and the first 200 lines or 25KB load each session.

12
00:00:56.307 --> 00:00:59.251
Glob, grep, and reads are the just-in-time half.

13
00:00:59.531 --> 00:01:04.181
That is why Claude Code can work in a large repository without loading it.

14
00:01:04.461 --> 00:01:09.432
Compaction happens automatically near the limit, and you can trigger it with /compact.

15
00:01:09.712 --> 00:01:19.675
The Agent SDK docs warn that compaction can lose specific instructions from early in a conversation, and recommend putting persistent rules in CLAUDE.

16
00:01:19.955 --> 00:01:23.539
md, which is re-injected, rather than in a first message.

17
00:01:23.819 --> 00:01:25.803
You can also add a section to CLAUDE.

18
00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:28.472
md telling the compactor what to preserve.

19
00:01:28.752 --> 00:01:30.885
Subagents are the isolation half.

20
00:01:31.165 --> 00:01:39.720
Built-in ones such as Explore (read-only search) and Plan run in their own context windows and return a summary; you can define your own in.

21
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.544
claude/agents/ with a description, an allowed tool list, and a model.

22
00:01:44.824 --> 00:01:50.904
A subagent starts fresh and does not see your conversation, so the task you give it must stand on its own.

23
00:01:51.184 --> 00:01:53.701
Practical habits that follow: keep CLAUDE.

24
00:01:53.981 --> 00:02:04.904
md short and about rules, not history; send broad searches to a subagent; and start a fresh session for an unrelated task rather than dragging an old context along.
